-- title:
--   Branch primes at a crossing: Gauss criterion and evaluation
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that maps to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and the hypothesis $\mathrm{jqModC}\ \mathbb{Q} \in \mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb{Q}\ \top$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : R_p \to A$ be the structure map (its composite with $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $\mathrm{algebraMap}$, and $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,(R_p)\,A = \rho$). Let $\theta$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{F}_H =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` which, by `hwgen`, induces on places the map realised by $\mathfrak{X}.w$: whenever $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y, y'$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ over the base satisfy $y' \cdot \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta} \cdot \mathrm{pullback.fst} \cdot \mathfrak{X}.w.\mathrm{hom} = y \cdot \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta} \cdot \mathrm{pullback.fst}$ (composition in diagrammatic order), then the place of $y'$ is the image of the place of $y$ under the semilinear automorphism attached to $\theta$. Put $T = A \otimes_{R_p} \mathcal{O}$ with $\mathcal{O} =$ `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj`, and let $\gamma : T \to \overline{F}_H$ be a ring homomorphism sending $a \otimes b$ to $a \cdot \mathrm{coeffEmb}(b)$ on Laurent series. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ A\ hA\ \rho\ h\rho\ 0$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ A\ hA\ \rho\ h\rho\ 1$, and let $\mathfrak{Q} \subset T$ be a prime which is the kernel of a ring homomorphism $\chi_\kappa : T \to \kappa$ restricting on $A$ to the residue map, and which is the prime of $n$ in the sense that some $\kappa$-point $t$ of the fibre over $(\mathrm{residue}) \circ \rho$ satisfies $t \cdot \mathrm{pullback.fst} = \mathrm{Spec}(\chi_\kappa) \cdot \mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{includeRight}) \cdot \iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, $t \cdot \mathrm{pullback.snd} = \mathrm{id}$, and $t$ carries the closed point to the image of $n$ under the first projection followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ A\ hA\ \rho\ h\rho\ 0$. The conclusion asserts the existence of two primes $\mathfrak{r}_0, \mathfrak{r}_1$ of $T$, both contained in $\mathfrak{Q}$ and incomparable, such that the ideal of $T$ generated by the maximal ideal of $A$ equals $\mathfrak{r}_0 \cap \mathfrak{r}_1$; such that for every $h \in \overline{F}_H$ one has $h \in \gamma(T)_{\mathfrak{r}_0}$ (i.e. $h\gamma(c) = \gamma(a)$ for some $a, c \in T$ with $c \notin \mathfrak{r}_0$) if and only if $h$ is a ratio $x/y$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose denominator has nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, and the same equivalence for $\mathfrak{r}_1$ with $\theta h$ in place of $h$; and such that, for all $h$ and all $a, c \in T$ with $c \notin \mathfrak{Q}$ and $h\gamma(c) = \gamma(a)$, whenever $x, y$ are Laurent series over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction and $h \cdot y = x$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficients, every $g \in \mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ (\Gamma_N\,p\,M\,H)$ with $g \cdot \bar{y} = \bar{x}$ lies in the valuation ring of the place $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{placeOn0}\ A\ hA\ \rho\ h\rho\ n$ (the Frobenius place `qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL` of the supersingular place $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{nodeEquiv}\ A\ hA\ \rho\ h\rho\ n$) with residue $\chi_\kappa(a)/\chi_\kappa(c)$, and correspondingly, with $\theta h$ in place of $h$, the value $\chi_\kappa(a)/\chi_\kappa(c)$ is taken at the place $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{placeOn1}\ A\ hA\ \rho\ h\rho\ n$ (that supersingular place itself).
--
--   This is the local analysis at a supersingular crossing of the special fibre at $p$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$: the two branches through the crossing are identified with the Gauss prolongation at the cusp and its transform under the Atkin–Lehner automorphism $\theta$, and a function regular at the crossing is evaluated there on both components. It feeds [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_primes_tensorProduct_chartAlgFin_crossing_gauss_iff_and_section_and_hasValue`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_primes_tensorProduct_chartAlgFin_crossing_gauss_iff_and_section_and_hasValue).
